---
const items = [
  {
    key: "runtime flags",
    desc: "decide which tools exist at all this run: <code>--web</code>, <code>--shell</code>, attended vs. headless."
  },
  {
    key: "session mode",
    desc: "Plan grants no mutation tools; Build opens edits, writes, and shell. A grant cannot override a mode."
  },
  {
    key: "permission policy",
    desc: "each request is accepted, asked about, or rejected, and re-checked immediately before it runs."
  }
];
---

<section class="permissions" id="permissions" aria-labelledby="perm-h">
  <p class="section-label" id="perm-h">Permissions</p>
  <p class="block-intro">
    Reads inside your repo are automatic. Edits and writes are automatic in
    Build. Anything outside the trusted root asks first, and one grant covers
    that directory and everything beneath it for the session.
  </p>
  <div class="tui-panel policy">
    <ul class="policy-list">
      {
        items.map((it) => (
          <li class="policy-item">
            <span class="hl-yellow">{it.key}</span>
            <span class="policy-desc set:html={it.desc}" />
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
